# 043026 - Daily Work Log

## Decisions
- Project-driven Rust learning: build a real application together.
- Coaching rule: pseudocode/scaffolding by default; full real code only when user asks to refine/finish or as a review example.
- Tooling: git from day one, rust-analyzer, cargo-watch, CI/CD planned.
- **Project name:** nimbus (Goku's cloud — future cluster could be nimbus.cloud).
- **Domain:** Distributed KV with stream/queue/cluster ambitions (Option B). Niche deferred to ~M4.
- **M1 design (all 6 steps):** commands `get/set/del/exists/incr/decr`; `enum Command` + match dispatch; apply-mutation `Storage` trait with `Mutation` + `MutationOutcome`; Layout 2 modules (`cmd/storage/executor/repl/error.rs` + `lib.rs` + `main.rs`); per-module errors with hand-rolled `ParseError` + thiserror `StorageError` + anyhow `main.rs`; plain stdin REPL input (generic over `BufRead`/`Write`); **Heavy + TDD testing strategy with proptest, ~35–50 tests, CI from first commit.**
- Acronym-explain rule: spell out every technical acronym on first use until told to stop.
- Multi-choice option presentation: prefer `AskUserQuestion` over raw text bullets.

